"use strict";(self.webpackChunkdocs=self.webpackChunkdocs||[]).push([[2015],{79128:e=>{e.exports=JSON.parse('{"functions":[{"name":"new","desc":"Constructs a round. Called by a subclass\'s own `.new`, which then\\nre-`setmetatable`s the result onto itself.\\n\\nMerges `config` over `MinigameConfig.default`, picks the map (`props.map` if\\ngiven, otherwise a random entry from `config.maps`), and calls\\n[BaseGameMode:Setup] to clone it into the world. The round is **not** live\\nyet \u2014 [BaseGameMode:Start] does that.\\n\\nIt also installs three lifetime handlers, all owned by the round\'s Maid:\\n\\n- **`PlayerAdded`** \u2014 a player joining mid-round waits for their character,\\n  then receives the current countdown, the game music cue and the round-start\\n  state, so a late joiner\'s HUD matches everyone else\'s.\\n- **`PlayerRemoving`** \u2014 removes the leaver from the round and their team.\\n- **`TEAM_JOIN` / `TEAM_LEAVE`** \u2014 lets a client switch teams mid-round;\\n  joining also spawns the player at their new team\'s spawn.\\n\\nGamepass ownership is scanned on a background thread rather than inline,\\nbecause `GamePass.has` yields per player and the round must not block on it.\\nThe scan only runs if the lobby met the minimum player count.","params":[{"name":"config","desc":"The mode\'s own config","lua_type":"MinigameTypes.GameModeConfig"},{"name":"props","desc":"Per-round overrides, e.g. a forced map","lua_type":"MinigameTypes.GameModeProps"}],"returns":[{"desc":"","lua_type":"BaseGameMode"}],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":292,"path":"src/Server/Class/BaseGameMode.luau"}},{"name":"SetLighting","desc":"Applies the mode\'s `config.lighting` block to the game\'s Lighting service \u2014\\nambient, brightness, clock time and the atmosphere settings. No-ops when the\\nmode declares no lighting.\\n\\nCalled on map setup and again in [BaseGameMode:Stop] to put the lighting back.\\n\\n:::caution\\nThe restore in `Stop` calls this same method, so it re-applies the *mode\'s*\\nlighting rather than the lobby\'s. A mode that changes lighting leaves it\\nchanged until the next mode overwrites it.\\n:::","params":[],"returns":[],"function_type":"method","source":{"line":466,"path":"src/Server/Class/BaseGameMode.luau"}},{"name":"FindPlayerTeam","desc":"Returns the name of the team a player is on, or `nil` if they are on none or\\nthe round has no teams.\\n\\nSearches the authoritative `teams` lists rather than reading the character\'s\\n`TeamTag` attribute, so it stays correct even if the character has been\\nreplaced.","params":[{"name":"player","desc":"","lua_type":"Player"}],"returns":[{"desc":"","lua_type":"string?"}],"function_type":"method","source":{"line":496,"path":"src/Server/Class/BaseGameMode.luau"}},{"name":"GetSpawn","desc":"Picks a random spawn point from the map\'s `Spawns` folder, or from the\\n`Spawns/<team>` sub-folder when a team is given.\\n\\nDegrades rather than erroring on a mis-authored map: with no `Spawns` folder\\nat all it warns and falls back to the map\'s PrimaryPart (or its first part), so\\na round still starts with everyone piled on the origin instead of failing.","params":[{"name":"team","desc":"Team name to spawn within","lua_type":"string?"}],"returns":[{"desc":"","lua_type":"BasePart"}],"function_type":"method","source":{"line":526,"path":"src/Server/Class/BaseGameMode.luau"}},{"name":"Spawn","desc":"Places one or more players at spawn points and returns the ones actually\\nplaced \u2014 a player who left, died during the call, or whose character could not\\nbe built is skipped, so **always check the returned list** before firing\\nfollow-up logic like `PlayerSpawned`.\\n\\n`spawns` accepts a single part, a list of parts, or a folder (whose BasePart\\nchildren are used); each player independently draws a random one. With\\n`loadCharacter` set, a fresh character model is built and assigned, which is\\nhow respawns work; otherwise the existing character is teleported.\\n\\nPlayers are scattered around their spawn point by a random offset, read from\\nthe spawn\'s `SpawnOffset` attribute (or a legacy `Offset` value object),\\ndefaulting to \xb14 studs \u2014 this is what stops a team spawning inside itself.\\n\\nEach spawned character is stamped with the round\'s attributes: `Spawned`, the\\n`RoundTag` round id, and the mode\'s `HealthRegen`, `UseFallDamage` and\\n`KeepRagdollInWorld` settings. A `Died` listener is attached that routes into\\n[BaseGameMode:HandlePlayerDeath].\\n\\nAborts and returns an empty list if the round stops mid-call, since character\\ncreation yields.\\n\\n**Yields** when building characters.","params":[{"name":"data","desc":"","lua_type":"{ players: Player | { Player }, spawns: Folder | BasePart | { BasePart }, loadCharacter: boolean? }"}],"returns":[{"desc":"Players successfully placed","lua_type":"{ Player }"}],"function_type":"method","source":{"line":570,"path":"src/Server/Class/BaseGameMode.luau"}},{"name":"RemovePlayer","desc":"Removes a player from the round (and from `team`, if given) and rebroadcasts\\nthe alive count.\\n\\nThis drops them from `players` but does **not** clear their winner entry,\\nscore or pending rewards \u2014 a player who has already won still gets paid if\\nthey leave, and their character is not touched.","params":[{"name":"player","desc":"","lua_type":"Player"},{"name":"team","desc":"Team to also remove them from","lua_type":"string?"}],"returns":[],"function_type":"method","source":{"line":708,"path":"src/Server/Class/BaseGameMode.luau"}},{"name":"HandlePlayerDeath","desc":"Handles a player dying. Wired up automatically by [BaseGameMode:Spawn]; modes\\nrarely call it directly.\\n\\nFirst, kill credit: if the character carries a `KillTag` attribute naming a\\nkiller\'s UserId, that killer is rewarded one `kills` point and `PlayerDied`\\nfires with both players. The tag is cleared so a body cannot be credited twice.\\n\\nThen a life is spent. With lives remaining the player waits\\n`config.respawnTime`, respawns at their team\'s spawn with a fresh character,\\nand is told their new life count. With none left they are removed from the\\nround, moved to `inactivePlayers`, and sent `PLAYER_INACTIVE` \u2014 they stay in\\nthe world as a spectator rather than being kicked back to the lobby mid-round.\\n\\n**Yields** for the respawn delay and character creation.","params":[{"name":"player","desc":"The player who died","lua_type":"Player"}],"returns":[],"function_type":"method","source":{"line":743,"path":"src/Server/Class/BaseGameMode.luau"}},{"name":"EnoughPlayers","desc":"Whether the round still has the globally required minimum number of players\\n(`MinigameConfig.minimumPlayers`, not the mode\'s own `config.minimumPlayers`).\\n\\nWhen it fails, it optionally announces the shortfall and \u2014 if a map is\\nloaded \u2014 stops the round. So this is not a pure predicate: calling it can end\\nthe round.\\n\\nCall it after any yield, since players can leave while a mode is waiting.","params":[{"name":"broadcastMessage","desc":"Announce the shortfall to players","lua_type":"boolean?"}],"returns":[{"desc":"","lua_type":"boolean"}],"function_type":"method","source":{"line":827,"path":"src/Server/Class/BaseGameMode.luau"}},{"name":"PlayerCheck","desc":"Whether the round should keep going. Consulted every tick of\\n[BaseGameMode:GameCountdown] and after every [BaseGameMode:AddWinner].\\n\\nReturns `false` when the round is not playing, when nobody is left, or when\\n**every remaining player is already a winner** \u2014 the last being the \\"everyone\\nmade it, nothing left to play for\\" exit. Set `config.disableWinnerCheck` to\\nskip that test entirely, which is what modes need when every participant is\\nexpected to win.\\n\\nThe all-winners test is a loop rather than a `#players == #winners`\\ncomparison, deliberately: players can die and still be winners, so the two\\ncounts drift apart and only a membership scan is correct. If any non-winner is\\nfound, the round continues provided the mode\'s own `config.minimumPlayers` is\\nstill met.","params":[],"returns":[{"desc":"`true` to continue the round","lua_type":"boolean"}],"function_type":"method","source":{"line":871,"path":"src/Server/Class/BaseGameMode.luau"}},{"name":"GiveWeapon","desc":"murder-escape addition (not in core): gives each player a Gearkit gear\\n(the `firebit-dev/gearkit` package), equipped, wearing their equipped skin.","params":[{"name":"players","desc":"","lua_type":"Player | { Player }"},{"name":"weapon","desc":"Gear id under `Shared/Data/Gear`","lua_type":"string"},{"name":"mods","desc":"Attributes set on each gear\'s Tool","lua_type":"{ [string]: any }?"}],"returns":[{"desc":"The last Tool given, so the mode can modify it","lua_type":"Tool?"}],"function_type":"method","source":{"line":919,"path":"src/Server/Class/BaseGameMode.luau"}},{"name":"TeamSetup","desc":"Creates the round\'s teams from a `{ name \u2192 Color3 }` map, each starting empty.\\nCalled automatically by [BaseGameMode:Start] when `config.teams` is set; a mode\\nonly calls it directly to build teams dynamically.\\n\\nUntil this runs `self.teams` is `nil`, which is how the rest of the class tells\\na team round from a free-for-all.","params":[{"name":"teamCfg","desc":"Team names to their colours","lua_type":"{ [string]: Color3 }"}],"returns":[],"function_type":"method","source":{"line":966,"path":"src/Server/Class/BaseGameMode.luau"}},{"name":"TeamPlayerIndex","desc":"Index of a player within a team\'s roster, or `nil` if they are not on it.\\nMostly an internal helper for [BaseGameMode:TeamRemove].","params":[{"name":"player","desc":"","lua_type":"Player"},{"name":"teamName","desc":"","lua_type":"string"}],"returns":[{"desc":"","lua_type":"number?"}],"function_type":"method","source":{"line":988,"path":"src/Server/Class/BaseGameMode.luau"}},{"name":"TeamRemove","desc":"Removes a player from a team\'s roster. Asserts that teams have been set up.\\n\\nOnly touches the roster \u2014 the character\'s `TeamTag` attribute and overhead\\ncolour are left as they were. Use [BaseGameMode:TeamPush] to move a player\\nbetween teams, which keeps both in sync.","params":[{"name":"player","desc":"","lua_type":"Player"},{"name":"teamName","desc":"","lua_type":"string"}],"returns":[],"function_type":"method","source":{"line":1013,"path":"src/Server/Class/BaseGameMode.luau"}},{"name":"TeamPush","desc":"Adds players to a team, **moving** them off their current team first if they\\nhave one. The supported way to assign or reassign team membership.\\n\\nKeeps the three pieces of team state in step: the roster list, the character\'s\\n`TeamTag` attribute, and the overhead nameplate colour. Players without a\\ncharacter are skipped, since `TeamTag` has nowhere to live.\\n\\nAsserts that teams exist and that `teamName` is one of them.","params":[{"name":"players","desc":"","lua_type":"Player | { Player }"},{"name":"teamName","desc":"Destination team","lua_type":"string"}],"returns":[],"function_type":"method","source":{"line":1039,"path":"src/Server/Class/BaseGameMode.luau"}},{"name":"TeamAssignPlayers","desc":"Distributes the round\'s players across all teams, invoking `playerCallback`\\nfor each assignment so a mode can apply per-team setup as it goes.\\n\\n:::caution\\nThe distribution is `i % teamIndex == 0` with `teamIndex` starting at 1, so the\\nfirst team matches *every* player and later teams claim overlapping subsets.\\nPlayers are consequently assigned more than once, with the last write winning \u2014\\nthe in-file TODO acknowledges this. Do not rely on it for balanced teams;\\nassign explicitly with [BaseGameMode:TeamPush] when balance matters.\\n:::","params":[{"name":"playerCallback","desc":"Called per assignment","lua_type":"((player: Player, teamName: string, teamColor: Color3) -> ())?"}],"returns":[],"function_type":"method","source":{"line":1088,"path":"src/Server/Class/BaseGameMode.luau"}},{"name":"AddPoint","desc":"Adds (or subtracts, with a negative) raw score for a player. Score feeds the\\nend-of-round ranking only \u2014 it is **not** a payout. Use\\n[BaseGameMode:Reward] for anything the player should actually receive.","params":[{"name":"player","desc":"","lua_type":"Player"},{"name":"diff","desc":"Points to add","lua_type":"number"}],"returns":[],"function_type":"method","source":{"line":1136,"path":"src/Server/Class/BaseGameMode.luau"}},{"name":"SetRewardMultiplier","desc":"Sets a per-player payout multiplier, applied at `Stop` to both their rewards\\nand their final score. Intended for placement bonuses \u2014 first finisher gets\\nmore than second, and so on.\\n\\nPassing `nil` resets it to 1.","params":[{"name":"player","desc":"","lua_type":"Player"},{"name":"multiplier","desc":"Defaults to 1","lua_type":"number?"}],"returns":[],"function_type":"method","source":{"line":1154,"path":"src/Server/Class/BaseGameMode.luau"}},{"name":"Reward","desc":"Accumulates rewards for a player: `{ coins = 10, xp = 5 }` and so on. Values\\nadd to whatever the player has already earned this round.\\n\\nAny stat that appears in `MinigameConfig.pointValues` **also** adds to the\\nplayer\'s score, at that stat\'s configured rate. That coupling is why most modes\\nonly ever call `Reward` and never touch [BaseGameMode:AddPoint] directly.\\n\\nRewards are banked, not granted \u2014 nothing reaches the player\'s profile until\\n`Stop`, and only if they are a winner.","params":[{"name":"player","desc":"","lua_type":"Player"},{"name":"changes","desc":"Stat names to amounts to add","lua_type":"{ [string]: number }"}],"returns":[],"function_type":"method","source":{"line":1182,"path":"src/Server/Class/BaseGameMode.luau"}},{"name":"GetNumberOfWinners","desc":"How many players have been declared winners so far. Useful for placement\\nlogic \u2014 a mode typically reads this before adding the next winner to work out\\ntheir rank.","params":[],"returns":[{"desc":"","lua_type":"number"}],"function_type":"method","source":{"line":1219,"path":"src/Server/Class/BaseGameMode.luau"}},{"name":"AddWinner","desc":"Declares one or more players winners of the round. Winning is what makes a\\nplayer eligible for payout at `Stop`.\\n\\nEach new winner is immediately granted the mode\'s configured `reward.coins`\\nand `reward.xp`. Players already recorded as winners, or who are no longer in\\nthe round, are skipped.\\n\\n:::caution\\n**This can end the round.** After each winner is added, [BaseGameMode:PlayerCheck]\\nruns, and if every remaining player is now a winner the round stops\\nimmediately. Modes where all participants eventually win must set\\n`config.disableWinnerCheck`.\\n:::","params":[{"name":"players","desc":"","lua_type":"Player | { Player }"}],"returns":[],"function_type":"method","source":{"line":1243,"path":"src/Server/Class/BaseGameMode.luau"}},{"name":"RemoveWinner","desc":"Revokes winner status, for modes where winning can be lost again.\\n\\nDoes **not** claw back the coins and xp [BaseGameMode:AddWinner] already\\nbanked into the player\'s rewards; it only removes them from the payout list, so\\nthe net effect is that they receive nothing.\\n\\n:::caution\\nReturns on the *first* successful removal rather than processing the whole\\nlist, so passing multiple players only removes one of them.\\n:::","params":[{"name":"players","desc":"","lua_type":"Player | { Player }"}],"returns":[{"desc":"Whether a winner was removed","lua_type":"Types.Success"}],"function_type":"method","source":{"line":1293,"path":"src/Server/Class/BaseGameMode.luau"}},{"name":"_dispatchRoundStart","desc":"Broadcasts `ROUND_START` with the round\'s participant list. Sent to everyone,\\nincluding spectators, so all clients can render the round HUD.\\n\\nAlso re-sent to a single late joiner (with the same full list) so their HUD\\ncatches up.","params":[{"name":"players","desc":"Defaults to the round\'s current players","lua_type":"{ Player }?"}],"returns":[],"function_type":"method","private":true,"source":{"line":1329,"path":"src/Server/Class/BaseGameMode.luau"}},{"name":"_dispatchAliveCount","desc":"Broadcasts the number of players still in the round, driving the client\'s\\nalive-count display.","params":[],"returns":[],"function_type":"method","private":true,"source":{"line":1346,"path":"src/Server/Class/BaseGameMode.luau"}},{"name":"Announce","desc":"Shows a transient hint banner to **everyone** in the server, spectators\\nincluded. Use for round-wide narration (\\"30 seconds left!\\").\\n\\nCompare [BaseGameMode:Message], which is a larger, targetable message.","params":[{"name":"text","desc":"","lua_type":"string"},{"name":"timeout","desc":"Seconds before it fades; nil uses the client default","lua_type":"number?"}],"returns":[],"function_type":"method","source":{"line":1366,"path":"src/Server/Class/BaseGameMode.luau"}},{"name":"Message","desc":"Shows a header/body screen message. Unlike [BaseGameMode:Announce] this is\\ntargetable: pass `true` for everyone, or a player or list of players.","params":[{"name":"players","desc":"`true` broadcasts","lua_type":"boolean | Player | { Player }"},{"name":"header","desc":"","lua_type":"string?"},{"name":"body","desc":"","lua_type":"string?"}],"returns":[],"function_type":"method","source":{"line":1389,"path":"src/Server/Class/BaseGameMode.luau"}},{"name":"Countdown","desc":"Starts a client-side countdown display for the round\'s players and remembers\\nthe label so a late joiner can be shown the same thing.\\n\\nThis is display only \u2014 it drives no logic. [BaseGameMode:GameCountdown] is the\\none that actually times the round (and calls this for you).","params":[{"name":"duration","desc":"Seconds","lua_type":"number"},{"name":"text","desc":"Label shown beside the timer","lua_type":"string?"}],"returns":[],"function_type":"method","source":{"line":1417,"path":"src/Server/Class/BaseGameMode.luau"}},{"name":"DropCoin","desc":"Drops a physical collectible coin into the map at the given CFrame, with a\\nrandom spin and a downward nudge.\\n\\nThe coin plays an impact sound the first time it touches anything, and awards\\n4\u20138 coins to the first player who touches it before destroying itself. It is\\nparented to the map, so it disappears with the map at round end.","params":[{"name":"CFrame","desc":"Where to spawn the coin","lua_type":"CFrame"}],"returns":[],"function_type":"method","source":{"line":1442,"path":"src/Server/Class/BaseGameMode.luau"}},{"name":"SetPlayerSpeed","desc":"Sets a player\'s walk speed, or restores the game default when `walkSpeed` is\\nomitted. No-ops if they have no humanoid.\\n\\nNot reset automatically at round end \u2014 the character reload in `Stop` is what\\nclears it.","params":[{"name":"player","desc":"","lua_type":"Player"},{"name":"walkSpeed","desc":"Defaults to `Util.defaultWalkSpeed`","lua_type":"number?"}],"returns":[],"function_type":"method","source":{"line":1492,"path":"src/Server/Class/BaseGameMode.luau"}},{"name":"Loop","desc":"Runs `fn` repeatedly on a new thread until it returns a falsy value or the\\nround stops. Returns immediately \u2014 this does **not** yield the caller, so a\\nmode\'s `Play` cannot use it as its only body without also yielding some other\\nway.\\n\\n:::caution\\n`fn` **must yield at least one frame per iteration**. It is called in a tight\\n`while` loop with no implicit wait, so a non-yielding function hangs the\\nthread.\\n:::\\n\\n```lua\\nself:Loop(function()\\n\\ttask.wait(1)\\n\\treturn self:PlayerCheck()\\nend)\\n```","params":[{"name":"fn","desc":"Return truthy to keep looping","lua_type":"() -> boolean?"}],"returns":[],"function_type":"method","source":{"line":1532,"path":"src/Server/Class/BaseGameMode.luau"}},{"name":"GameCountdown","desc":"Runs the round timer and **yields until it finishes**. The usual body of a\\nmode\'s `Play`.\\n\\nCounts down from `duration` (defaulting to `config.roundTime`), starting the\\nclient-side display via [BaseGameMode:Countdown] and stepping `self.time` every\\nframe. `conditionCheck` \u2014 if given \u2014 is called roughly **once a second**, not\\nevery frame, and returning anything but `true` ends the countdown early.\\n\\nIt exits when any of these becomes true: the condition failed, the time ran\\nout, [BaseGameMode:PlayerCheck] said stop, or the round is no longer playing.\\nThe return value distinguishes the first case from the rest.\\n\\nWarns and returns immediately if the round has no config.","params":[{"name":"duration","desc":"Seconds; defaults to `config.roundTime`","lua_type":"number?"},{"name":"conditionCheck","desc":"Per-second check; return false to end early","lua_type":"((deltaTime: number) -> boolean)?"}],"returns":[{"desc":"`true` if the countdown completed with the condition intact","lua_type":"boolean"}],"function_type":"method","source":{"line":1569,"path":"src/Server/Class/BaseGameMode.luau"}},{"name":"Setup","desc":"Clones the named map out of `ServerStorage.Maps`, applies the mode\'s lighting,\\nand parents the clone into the Workspace as `GameContainer`.\\n\\nCalled by [BaseGameMode.new]; modes should not call it. The parenting is\\ndeferred to its own thread so a heavy map does not stall construction.","params":[{"name":"mapToLoad","desc":"Map name, matching a child of `ServerStorage.Maps`","lua_type":"string"}],"returns":[],"function_type":"method","private":true,"source":{"line":1631,"path":"src/Server/Class/BaseGameMode.luau"}},{"name":"Start","desc":"Runs the round from beginning to end and **yields for its entire duration**.\\nCalled by [GameService]; modes should not call it.\\n\\nIn order:\\n\\n1. Refresh the player list (people join during voting), and bail out via\\n   `Stop` if the mode\'s minimum is not met.\\n2. Per player: drop anyone dead or characterless, assign lives, optionally\\n   hide nameplates, stamp the `RoundTag`, and hide their equipped cosmetic.\\n   Dropping players re-checks the minimum as it goes.\\n3. Build teams from `config.teams` if present.\\n4. Call the subclass\'s `Init`, wrapped so a throw only warns.\\n5. Set `playing`, then auto-spawn if `config.autoSpawn` \u2014 per team into\\n   `Spawns/<teamName>` when teams exist, falling back to the shared `Spawns`\\n   folder if the map has no team spawns.\\n6. Call the subclass\'s `Play` (which yields for the round), or run a default\\n   [BaseGameMode:GameCountdown] if the mode does not define one.\\n7. `Stop`, unless the round already stopped itself.\\n\\n**Yields** for the whole round.","params":[],"returns":[],"function_type":"method","source":{"line":1676,"path":"src/Server/Class/BaseGameMode.luau"}},{"name":"Stop","desc":"Ends the round: pays out winners, shows the summary, and cleans up. Safe to\\ncall from anywhere, including from inside a mode \u2014 [BaseGameMode:Start] checks\\nwhether the round already stopped before calling it again.\\n\\nWorld teardown runs on its own thread with a 3-second grace period so players\\nsee the final moment before the map vanishes; lighting is restored and the map\\ndestroyed after it.\\n\\nThen, on the main path: fire `Stopping`, clear `playing`, fire `Stopped`,\\ndestroy the Maid (killing every round connection), broadcast `ROUND_END` and\\nstop the music. Cosmetics are restored for active and inactive players alike,\\nand every character carrying a `RoundTag` is reloaded.\\n\\nPayout, after a short beat, per winner:\\n\\n1. Apply `config.reward.multiplier` \xd7 the player\'s own\\n   [BaseGameMode:SetRewardMultiplier].\\n2. Apply the Premium multiplier to `xp` for Premium members.\\n3. Apply every gameplay gamepass multiplier the player owns, per stat.\\n4. Emit an [EndWinner] with the final rewards and score.\\n\\nWinners are then sorted by score to assign ranks, the whole table is broadcast\\nas `GAME_ROUND_SUMMARY` (each client also receiving its own local rewards), and\\ncoins, xp, points, kills and a win are written to each winner\'s profile.\\n\\nFinally calls [BaseGameMode:Destroy].\\n\\n**Yields** for several seconds across the teardown.","params":[],"returns":[],"function_type":"method","source":{"line":1843,"path":"src/Server/Class/BaseGameMode.luau"}},{"name":"Destroy","desc":"Final teardown: fires `Destroying` and destroys the Maid. Guarded so it only\\never runs once, since [BaseGameMode:Stop] calls it and callers may too.\\n\\nDoes not touch the map or the players \u2014 [BaseGameMode:Stop] owns that.","params":[],"returns":[],"function_type":"method","source":{"line":2010,"path":"src/Server/Class/BaseGameMode.luau"}}],"properties":[],"types":[{"name":"BaseGameMode","desc":"Instance shape of a round. Subclasses may add their own fields freely; `stats`\\nexists for modes that only need a scratch table and no new type.","fields":[{"name":"id","lua_type":"string","desc":"Unique round id; stamped on characters as `RoundTag`"},{"name":"players","lua_type":"{ Player }","desc":"Players still in the round"},{"name":"inactivePlayers","lua_type":"{ Player }","desc":"Players who ran out of lives and returned to the lobby"},{"name":"playerLives","lua_type":"{ [Player]: number }","desc":"Remaining lives per player"},{"name":"playerRewards","lua_type":"State","desc":"UserId to `{ stat: amount }`, the pending payout"},{"name":"rewardMultipliers","lua_type":"{ [Player]: number }","desc":"Per-player payout multiplier (placement bonuses)"},{"name":"scores","lua_type":"{ [Player]: number }","desc":"Raw score, used for end-of-round ranking"},{"name":"playerPassesOwned","lua_type":"{ [Player]: { string } }","desc":"Gameplay gamepass names, scanned at construction"},{"name":"stats","lua_type":"{ [Player]: any }","desc":"Free-form per-player scratch space for modes"},{"name":"winners","lua_type":"{ [UserId]: Player }","desc":"Declared winners; only these are paid"},{"name":"teams","lua_type":"{ [TeamName]: MinigameTypes.RoundTeam }?","desc":"nil in a free-for-all"},{"name":"playing","lua_type":"boolean","desc":"True between `Start` and `Stop`"},{"name":"time","lua_type":"number","desc":"Seconds remaining in the current countdown"},{"name":"countdownText","lua_type":"string?","desc":"Label shown alongside the countdown"},{"name":"map","lua_type":"Model?","desc":"The cloned map, parented as `GameContainer`"},{"name":"destroyed","lua_type":"boolean?","desc":"Guards `Destroy` against running twice"},{"name":"isWorldSetUp","lua_type":"boolean","desc":"Whether a map is currently loaded"},{"name":"config","lua_type":"MinigameTypes.GameModeConfig","desc":"Mode config merged over the defaults"},{"name":"intervalTime","lua_type":"number","desc":"Accumulator driving the once-a-second countdown callback"},{"name":"maid","lua_type":"Maid","desc":"Owns every connection made by the round"},{"name":"PlayerDied","lua_type":"Signal","desc":"(victim, killer?) \u2014 fired on a tagged kill"},{"name":"PlayerSpawned","lua_type":"Signal","desc":"(player, teamName?) \u2014 fired after a successful spawn"},{"name":"Stopping","lua_type":"Signal","desc":"Fired before the stop sequence begins"},{"name":"Stopped","lua_type":"Signal","desc":"Fired once the round is no longer playing"},{"name":"Destroying","lua_type":"Signal","desc":"Fired as the round tears down"}],"source":{"line":189,"path":"src/Server/Class/BaseGameMode.luau"}}],"name":"BaseGameMode","desc":"Full featured round base class for any type of round based experience.\\n\\nEverything a round needs \u2014 players, teams, scores, rewards, gamepass\\nmultipliers, map loading, lighting, spawning, the countdown, and the\\nend-of-round payout \u2014 lives here. A concrete game mode subclasses this and\\nsupplies only its own rules.\\n\\n## The subclass contract\\n\\nA game mode is a table that inherits from `BaseGameMode` and is constructed\\nwith a [GameModeConfig]. It implements **at most two** methods, both optional:\\n\\n| Method  | When it runs | Purpose |\\n| ------- | ------------ | ------- |\\n| `Init`  | after players are gathered, teams are set up and lives are assigned, but **before** `playing` is set and before auto-spawn | one-time round setup: wire signals, prepare the map, place props |\\n| `Play`  | after spawning, once the round is live | the round itself \u2014 **must yield for the whole round** |\\n\\nBoth are called by [BaseGameMode:Start], each wrapped in a `try` so a throwing\\nmode warns rather than wedging the server. When `Play` returns, the round is\\nover: `Start` calls [BaseGameMode:Stop] itself. A mode that omits `Play` gets\\nthe default behaviour of a plain [BaseGameMode:GameCountdown] for\\n`config.roundTime`.\\n\\n```lua\\nlocal MyMode = setmetatable({}, { __index = BaseGameMode })\\nMyMode.__index = MyMode\\n\\nfunction MyMode.new(props)\\n\\tlocal self = setmetatable(BaseGameMode.new(config, props), MyMode)\\n\\treturn self\\nend\\n\\nfunction MyMode.Init(self)\\n\\t-- one-time setup; the round is not live yet\\nend\\n\\nfunction MyMode.Play(self)\\n\\t-- yields for the whole round\\n\\tself:GameCountdown(nil, function()\\n\\t\\t-- runs once a second; return false to end the round early\\n\\t\\treturn true\\n\\tend)\\nend\\n```\\n\\nEverything else \u2014 `Setup`, `Start`, `Stop`, `Destroy` \u2014 is driven by\\n[GameService] and should not be overridden.\\n\\n## Round lifecycle\\n\\n1. **`new`** \u2014 merges the mode\'s config over `MinigameConfig.default`, picks a\\n   map, calls [BaseGameMode:Setup] to clone it in, snapshots the player list,\\n   and starts a background gamepass scan. Late joiners are caught by a\\n   `PlayerAdded` handler that re-sends the countdown, music and round-start\\n   state.\\n2. **`Start`** \u2014 refreshes the player list, drops anyone dead or characterless,\\n   assigns lives, hides cosmetics, sets up teams, runs `Init`, flips `playing`,\\n   auto-spawns if configured, then runs `Play`.\\n3. **The round** \u2014 the mode yields inside `Play`. Exits are: `Play` returning,\\n   [BaseGameMode:GameCountdown] running out or its condition returning false,\\n   [BaseGameMode:PlayerCheck] failing (too few players, or everybody has won),\\n   or an explicit `Stop`.\\n4. **`Stop`** \u2014 pays out winners, broadcasts the summary, reloads characters,\\n   restores lighting, destroys the map, and calls `Destroy`.\\n\\n## Winner semantics\\n\\n`winners` is a `UserId \u2192 Player` map, **not** a list of survivors. A mode\\ndeclares winners explicitly with [BaseGameMode:AddWinner]; nothing is implicit.\\nTwo consequences worth internalizing:\\n\\n- A player can be dead and still win \u2014 winning is recorded once and is not\\n  revoked by dying, only by [BaseGameMode:RemoveWinner].\\n- Because [BaseGameMode:PlayerCheck] ends the round once *every remaining\\n  player* is a winner, adding the last winner ends the round. Modes where\\n  everyone eventually wins (races, collection games) must set\\n  `config.disableWinnerCheck` or they will terminate the instant the field\\n  fills up.\\n\\n**Only winners are paid.** Scores are tracked for everyone but the payout loop\\nin `Stop` iterates `winners`, so a non-winner banks nothing.\\n\\n## Scoring and rewards\\n\\nTwo parallel notions:\\n\\n- **Score** \u2014 [BaseGameMode:AddPoint], a raw number used for end-of-round\\n  ranking.\\n- **Rewards** \u2014 [BaseGameMode:Reward], a per-player `{ stat \u2192 amount }` map\\n  (`coins`, `xp`, `kills`, \u2026) that becomes the actual payout. Any stat listed\\n  in `MinigameConfig.pointValues` *also* contributes to score at its configured\\n  rate, so most modes only call `Reward` and let score follow.\\n\\nAt payout, multipliers stack in this order: the mode\'s `config.reward.multiplier`\\n\xd7 the player\'s [BaseGameMode:SetRewardMultiplier] value, then Roblox Premium on\\n`xp`, then every gameplay gamepass the player owns. Rankings are assigned by\\nsorting on final score.\\n\\n## Teams\\n\\nOpt-in. Set `config.teams` to a `{ name \u2192 Color3 }` map and `Start` calls\\n[BaseGameMode:TeamSetup] automatically; otherwise `self.teams` stays `nil` and\\nthe round is a free-for-all. Team membership lives in two places that must stay\\nin sync \u2014 the `teams[name].players` list and the character\'s `TeamTag`\\nattribute \u2014 which is why [BaseGameMode:TeamPush] is the only supported way to\\nmove a player. Players may also join and leave teams at runtime via the\\n`TEAM_JOIN`/`TEAM_LEAVE` actions handled in the constructor.\\n\\nGated by [FeatureFlags].Minigames \u2014 disabled by default; per-project forks\\nenable it deliberately.\\n\\nCopyright (c) 2026 firebit. All rights reserved.\\nfirebit/murder-escape - proprietary and confidential.","tags":["dormant"],"realm":["Server"],"source":{"line":120,"path":"src/Server/Class/BaseGameMode.luau"}}')}}]);